-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Fourth Term Eq Split
-- statement:
--   **The fourth term splits by inserting the complete-part projector resolution.**
--
--   For every state, indexed polynomial family, and indexed projective submeasurement, write $G_q$ for the complete-part total at the first slice question, $M_o$ for the outcome-$o$ effect of the indexed submeasurement, and $P_q(g)$ for the family effect indexed by polynomial $g$. The fourth aggregate term equals
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{switcherooAggregateFourthTerm}
--   =\mathbb E_q\sum_{(g,o)}\left\langle G_qM_oP_q(g)P_q(g)M_o\right\rangle.
--   $$
--
--   The split is obtained from the complete-part resolution $G_q=\sum_g P_q(g)$. It exposes the polynomial index needed by the contraction and square-root estimates in the fourth-term switcheroo chain.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateFourthTerm_eq_split`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
